A second, independent sourcing pass contradicted the first on gongche and on
kepatihan. Arbitrating between two delegated readers by picking one would be
exactly the failure this project exists to prevent, so the contested PDFs were
fetched and their text extracted and grepped directly (25-line zlib extractor
over FlateDecode streams; both documents grepped, not summarised). The errors
were in THIS artifact, not upstream.

**The citation is real.** Verbatim from the extracted text: *"Analytical
Approaches to World Music, Vol. 8, No. 2. Published December 7, 2020. Metrical
Structure and Freedom in Qin Music of the Chinese Literati, Chun-Yan Tse and
Chun-Fung Wong."* Eiso Chan's L2/22-206 is real too — *"Proposal to add 38
characters used for the Chinese traditional musical notation to UAX #45"*,
2022-09-19.

**Two claims it does not support:**

* **Gongche → UNSOURCED.** The paper's subject is METRICAL structure; gongche
  appears once, in passing, for ban/yan pulse marks "adjacent to musical notes
  in gongche notation". It says nothing about movable degrees or skeletal
  status. The second pass independently reported gongche as unverified, so all
  three routes now agree. The row is retained as an EXPLICIT GAP rather than
  deleted, so the table cannot silently look complete.

* **F24's anchor → UNSOURCED, claim RETRACTED.** The jianzipu
  position-inheritance rule is ABSENT from both cited documents: 0 hits for
  persist / inherit / carry over / previous character / preceding character /
  omitted / abbreviat across 417 KB of extracted text. F24 is reframed from "a
  measurement of an attested rule" to a CONDITIONAL structural result — IF a
  notation carries reading state, THEN the atlas language does not reach it —
  with the antecedent claimed of no tradition. The consequent is what bounds
  the design and it survives either way, because it is a statement about what
  the atlas language can express.

**One row gets STRONGER, and it is the one F23 rests on.** Verbatim,
self-extracted: *"the tablature score used for the qin notates the fingering
... By following these fingering instructions, the player produces a musical
note."* Pitch-as-OUTPUT is now the best-attested claim in the table — new tier
VERIFIED-SELF, the only tier not taken on report.

Also folded in from the second pass: Byzantine is CONTEXTUALIZED as well as
intervallic, and its pre-1814 layers were stenographic; the maqam
staff-notation date is PROVISIONAL (1932 refuted, early-19th-c. not yet
attested — Popper unfetchable); al-Farabi's abjad notation IS sourced
(Camprubi 2022) while the wider chain is not; sargam needs BOTH halves —
artist-chosen AND fixed for the concert — or it misleads; Bozkurt et al. 2009
RANKS tuning models and must not be cited for blanket divergence. Kepatihan is
marked CONTESTED, neither promoted nor discarded.

Final tiers across 10 instances: 6 VERIFIED-OA, 1 VERIFIED-SELF, 1 EXPERT-WEB,
1 CONTESTED, 1 UNSOURCED — and zero unsourced claims stated as fact.

